-- title:
--   Polynomial separation data for the row-9 inverse cubic
-- statement:
--   These are explicit finite coefficient data for the degree-9 inverse cubic of a fifth power of $z^3-z-\beta$. The algebraic parameter used in the later proofs satisfies $\alpha^3=1001/2-462\alpha+84\alpha^2$. If the $j$th coefficient of $P_\alpha$ is $a_j+b_j\alpha+c_j\alpha^2$, the difference coefficients are $b_j+c_j\sigma$, where $\sigma$ is the sum of two real algebraic parameters. The bundle defines the 31 difference coefficients and three rational bound arrays, one for each pair of root intervals.
--
--   They are used to prove
--   $$|P_b(t)-P_a(t)-(b-a)|\le\tfrac9{10}(b-a)$$
--   on the row's stated reciprocal-radius disk. Together with the separately bounded analytic corrections, this separates the inverse branches. The inequality is proved in theorem submissions, not presumed by the arrays.
-- source:
--   https://gist.github.com/Amal-David/adce933460b7501cb123f483f62775eb/f5a76eda649f3e995a8ec6b98387b23b64c6debb#file-fifth-md; H5_COMPLETE_CHAIN.md, Sections 1–4; lower/H5_LOWER_MIDDLE_COMPLETION.md and upper/H5_UPPER_BRIDGE.md in the archived research checkpoint. The finite Newton coefficient arrays are auxiliary exact certificates constructed for the accompanying Lean formalization, and are specified in full by this definition submission.

